cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the accompanying paper. The paper is
  under review, so no DOI or volume is given here yet; update this file once
  the article is published.
title: >-
  Hierarchical Trustworthiness Evaluation for Distributed Multi-Agent Systems:
  A DLT-Based Governance Framework Evaluated in Federated Learning
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and experiment drivers for a DLT-based governance
  framework that evaluates agent trustworthiness through a 3-12-36 taxonomy of
  three levels, 12 categories and 36 control points, evaluated in a federated
  learning testbed.
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
